    "intro_html":  "Pollo guisado is the stew every Puerto Rican grandmother makes a little differently and every one of them insists hers is correct. Chicken braised down with sofrito, sazon, olives, potatoes and carrots until the broth turns into gravy and the potatoes start to fall apart on purpose. This is a big, generous pot. Each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost), and there is one line item driving that number that I want to talk about.",
